From: Leila Mitchell <leilamitchell@llmdesign.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:29:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] UX-016: the quantity leads, the sentence supports

A 44px glyph carries each role item's figure (days quiet, dollars at stake, a
limit breached, steps outstanding) coloured by the kind of signal; the sentence
sits beside it. Kind-of-source marks in front of every source line (TR-10).
Today's role cards, the next-two rows, and the four role overviews.

Where an item comes from a NextAction or Alert the figure is read back out of
the server's sentence, because the contract carries no structured figure. The
right fix is a lead field on NextAction and Alert; logged in UX_REQUESTS.

